-- Advance Database Management System | Mid 1 | easy | 440009351502011
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440009351502011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to functional dependency in the context of Functional Dependency and Decomposition. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Introduction to normalization in the context of Normalization. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Transaction concept in the context of Transaction and Concurrency. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain key terms for functional dependency in the context of Functional Dependency and Decomposition. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A functional dependency X→Y means each value of attribute set X determines a single value of Y in every valid row. Dependencies help identify keys, redundancy and suitable decompositions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to key terms for functional dependency; rules of functional dependency; types of functional dependency: Multivalued dependency; trivial functional dependency. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Normalization applies dependency-based rules to reduce redundancy and insertion, update and deletion anomalies. 1NF removes repeating groups, 2NF removes partial dependency on a candidate key, and 3NF/BCNF impose stronger dependency conditions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Normal Form: First Normal Form (1NF); Second Normal Form(2NF); Third Normal Form(3NF); Boyce Codd Normal Form(BCNF). State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concurrency control coordinates transactions that overlap in time. Locking controls access to data; correctness depends on lock compatibility, ordering and release, while poor locking can cause waiting or deadlocks.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to ACID property; basics of Concurrency; method of Concurrency control: Locking method; Timestamp method. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A functional dependency X→Y means each value of attribute set X determines a single value of Y in every valid row. Dependencies help identify keys, redundancy and suitable decompositions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Introduction to functional dependency; rules of functional dependency; types of functional dependency: Multivalued dependency; trivial functional dependency. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

