VALUES (440009351506011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Defining IoT in the context of Introduction to IoT. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Machine to Machine in the context of IoT & M2M. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Home automation in the context of Domain and Challenges in IoT. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Characteristics of IoT in the context of Introduction to IoT. Define it, describe key principles or steps and give one example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IoT connects physical devices, sensors and actuators through processing and communication. Security, reliability, connectivity and power constraints are central.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Characteristics of IoT; Physical design of Iot; Logical design of IoT; Functional blocks of IoT. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Machine-to-machine communication allows devices or systems to exchange data and coordinate actions automatically; IoT often includes a broader connected application ecosystem.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Difference between IoT and M2M; Software define Network; IoT & M2M. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IoT connects physical devices, sensors and actuators through processing and communication. Security, reliability, connectivity and power constraints are central.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Industry applications; Environment applications; Other IoT applications; Challenges in IoT. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IoT connects physical devices, sensors and actuators through processing and communication. Security, reliability, connectivity and power constraints are central.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Defining IoT; Physical design of Iot; Logical design of IoT; Functional blocks of IoT. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/s