ce.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** GSM is a 2G cellular system with radio access, subscriber identities, authentication, network elements and handover procedures.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to PLMN interface; addresses and identifiers; network aspects; frequency allocation. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Wireless LAN:- IEEE 802 and IEEE 802.11 Protocol Architecture appears in “Wireless Operations and its Standards”. Define its role, explain the main steps/components as taught, relate it to Services, Cellular Networks:- Channel allocation, multiple access, location management, give an example from the course, and note a validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Services; Cellular Networks:- Channel allocation; multiple access; location management. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Types appears in “What is Mobile Computing”. Define its role, explain the main steps/components as taught, relate it to History, Benefits, Application, Evolution, give an example from the course, and note a validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to History; Benefits; Application; Evolution. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

